  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: json 20220320.0.0.rhlw-00003",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released org.json:json 20220320.0.0.rhlw-00003 with backported fixes for CVE-2022-45688 and CVE-2023-5072.\n\nCVE-2022-45688: A stack overflow in the XML.toJSONObject component of org.json:json before version 20230227 allows attackers to cause a Denial of Service (DoS) via crafted JSON or XML data.\n\nCVE-2023-5072: A bug in the parser means that an input string of modest size can lead to indefinite amounts of memory being used, causing a Denial of Service (DoS).\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for org.json:json 20220320 from Maven Central.",
  "severity": [
    {
      "type": "CVSS_V3",
